**How to implement.** The rest of the UI suite names every seeded preset through `PresetIds` (.spec-md §3.3) while the ids still hold their step-15 text. Every occurrence in the files below, comments included, switches. Afterwards `git grep -n -E "(src|det|pol)-[a-z0-9]" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests` lists only test-local ids, which stay: the user sources "src-new-1", "src-x", "src-y", "src-u", "src-mine" and "src-typed" of `LightSourceEditorTests.fs`, "src-x" of `ScrollExtentTests.fs:149`, "src-test-10nm" of `FsxAcceptanceTests.fs` and "src-tune" of `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs:289-292`. A fixture holds an id as an `ElementValueId`, and a helper that wrapped a `string` id takes the `ElementValueId` (AGENTS.md 'Elevate at origin'). (1) `ElementRendererBindingTests.fs`: `drawableOf` (`:26-27`) takes `valueId : ElementValueId option`; `stateOf` (`:63-64`) follows, wrapping its test-local ids where it writes them (`Some (ElementValueId "lib:sample")`); the HideNormals fact (`:92`) draws `Some PresetIds.polarizerLp`. (2) `InverseConstructorTests.fs:155`: `PresetIds.detectorEllipsometer`. (3) `LightSourceEditorTests.fs:173`: `PresetIds.euv13p5`; `:210`: `PresetIds.arf193`. (4) `SolverHandoffWindowTests.fs`: `baseExperiment` (`:61`) takes `srcBind : ElementValueId option` and `detBind : ElementValueId option`, `bindOne` binds the id it receives, and every call (`:134-259`) passes `Some PresetIds.source600` with `Some PresetIds.detectorIntensity`, or `Some PresetIds.detectorEllipsometer` at `:182`. (5) `WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs:253-261` and `WireUiCompositionTests.fs:197`: `ConstructorUiId.libraryEntryNode PresetIds.source600`, `PresetIds.polarizerLp` and `PresetIds.polarizerCpLeft`. (6) `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs`: `bind` (`:40`) and `filmOnR2` (`:158`) take an `ElementValueId`; `glassFilm200Id` and `glassPlate1mmId` (`:41-42`) hold the sample's `entryId`; the binds and lookups read `PresetIds.heNe633` (`:68`, `:123-125`, `:176`, `:185`), `arf193` (`:79`), `krf248` (`:137`, `:150`), `xenonMonochromator` (`:167`, `:184`), `source600` (`:190`, `:254`), `detectorEllipsometer` (`:202`) and `detectorIntensity` (`:129`).

**Acceptance.** After the switch, ui-tests (ElementRendererBindingTests, InverseConstructorTests, LightSourceEditorTests, SolverHandoffWindowTests, WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests) and ui-smoke, which holds WireUi0040CompositionTests and WireUiCompositionTests, MUST pass with unchanged counts, every fact holding its assertion; and build, elevation and the five s03 invariants MUST pass.
